{"id":"BkiUeSbxK6-gD5TlegmE","content":"Norman John Goss (born 3 March 1951) is a former Australian rules footballer who played with South Melbourne and Hawthorn in the Victorian Football League (VFL).\n\nGoss was originally from Port Melbourne, the club that his father had played for. He was their best and fairest in back to back years, 1969 and 1970.\n\nIn 1972 Goss joined South Melbourne and in 1974 he won the Bob Skilton Medal for their best and fairest player and also topped their goalkicking for the year with 37 goals.\n\nHe moved to Hawthorn in 1978 and was a premiership player in his debut season.\n\nIn August 2003 he was selected in Port Melbourne's official 'Team of the Century'.\nNorm was chairman of selectors for Allan Jeans at Hawthorn and Stan Alves at StKilda.\n\nExternal links\n\n1951 births\nLiving people\nAustralian rules footballers from Victoria (Australia)\nSydney Swans players\nHawthorn Football Club players\nHawthorn Football Club Premiership players\nPort Melbourne Football Club players\nBob Skilton Medal winners\nOne-time VFL/AFL Premiership players","ad_en":[-3.607421875,4.0546875],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.0119760479041915,"fineweb_edu":[1.232504963874817],"modernbert_readability":[-8.453125,-5.2265625,-3.3828125,-1.51171875,7.171875,8.140625],"qurater":[-0.425048828125,-1.3251953125,3.267578125,-0.329833984375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":4.301075268817205,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":4.32333123,"dsir_math":-1263.6045096,"dsir_wiki":-1103.28739245,"rps_doc_num_sentences":8,"rps_doc_word_count":167.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.45703125,9.21875,6.68359375,-0.487548828125,-4.84375,-7.125],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":56.886227544910184,"fluency_en":[-3.3125,2.9765625],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":22.06025267249757,"dsir_books":-1181.9348013,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-10.8671875,-10.546875,5.4375,5.0703125,9.6484375,-5.98828125],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":33.18139941194284,"modernbert_reasoning":[6.265625,10.6171875,3.12695