{"id":"BkiUfcDxK7Tt6AlxF8n8","content":"Окръг Потър () е окръг в щата Пенсилвания, Съединени американски щати. Площта му е 2800 km², а населението - 16 802 души (2017). Административен център е град Каудърспорт.\n\nИзточници \n\nОкръзи в Пенсилвания","ad_en":[-1.94921875,2.369140625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.366666666666666,"fineweb_edu":[0.43012383580207825],"modernbert_readability":[-5.44921875,1.1943359375,0.5146484375,1.70703125,2.37109375,-2.146484375],"qurater":[-4.27734375,-2.673828125,-1.6318359375,-3.044921875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":0.0,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.15270672,"dsir_math":-368.57328282,"dsir_wiki":-366.80226645,"rps_doc_num_sentences":4,"rps_doc_word_count":30.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-2.751953125,6.12109375,4.16796875,-0.3046875,-2.400390625,-5.203125],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":83.33333333333334,"fluency_en":[1.4189453125,-1.19140625],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":99.02439024390245,"dsir_books":-374.03051656,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-8.171875,-8.328125,3.216796875,3.0078125,8.09375,-4.125],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":44.8187134502924,"modernbert_reasoning":[5.44921875,11.0390625,3.1953125,-5.0859375,-6.03125,-6.06640625],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":60.0,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":2.7253668763102725,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUazA5qhLAB70I2VEY","content":"Jorge Mariné (born 24 September 1941) is a Spanish former cyclist. He competed in the individual road race at the 1964 Summer Olympics.\n\nReferences\n\nExternal links\n \n\n1941 births\nLiving people\nSpanish male cyclists\nOlympic cyclists of Spain\nCyclists at the 1964 Summer Olympics\nPeople from Baix Camp\nSportspeople from the Province of Tarragona\nCyclists from Catalonia\n20th-century Spanish people","ad_en":[-3.865234375,4.4296875],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.559322033898305,"fineweb_edu":[0.4192071557044983],"modernbert_readability":[-9.625,-4.6484375,-3.703125,-0.50390625,5.21484375,9.40625],"qurater":[-2.818359375,-2.541015625,1.0625,-2.107421875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":3.048780487804878,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.58100131,"dsir_math":-549.8341074,"dsir_wiki":-514.71104881,"rps_doc_num_sentences":3,"rps_doc_word_count":59.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.900390625,10.84375,6.7890625,-0.85498046875,-4.72265625,-7.2890625],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":69.49152542372882,"fluency_en":[-1.498046875,1.5048828125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":22.531645569620252,"dsir_books":-539.40477539,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-9.6640625,-6.8984375,7.1875,5.828125,6.8671875,-9.78125],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":24.04858765406036,"modernbert_reasoning":[8.671875,10.5625,0.69921875,-5.66015625,-6.53515625,-6.32421875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":5,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":31.25,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":5.228567728567729,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUdb45qhLA6eZZncjn","content":"11B97 was a Soviet nuclear electric rocket engine developed from 1978 through 1986. It was designed with enough propellent to work for 16,000 hours and the nuclear reactor would have had three years of life. It would have been capable of moving up to 100 tonnes of mass to a geostationary orbit, but was never flown.\n\nSee also\n NERVA, the American project for nuclear thermal propulsion\n RD-0410\n\nReferences\n\nNuclear spacecraft propulsion","ad_en":[-3.671875,4.26171875],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.014084507042254,"fineweb_edu":[2.868929624557495],"modernbert_readability":[-8.6875,-5.41796875,-4.26953125,0.06805419921875,5.42578125,6.921875],"qurater":[-2.7421875,3.12890625,5.97265625,0.462646484375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":5.056179775280898,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.90864116,"dsir_math":-592.15261815,"dsir_wiki":-557.35046406,"rps_doc_num_sentences":4,"rps_doc_word_count":71.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-4.34375,1.0712890625,4.26953125,3.7265625,0.059234619140625,-4.93359375],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":77.46478873239437,"fluency_en":[-3.107421875,2.794921875],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":24.200913242009136,"dsir_books":-557.96415762,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-11.015625,-11.3984375,4.09375,4.83203125,9.7109375,-5.921875],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":40.26484335247809,"modernbert_reasoning":[0.1669921875,10.421875,5.59765625,-2.76171875,-5.08984375,-6.6953125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":44.44444444444444,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":12.18292247231154,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUdWI4ubnjoxKrZu52","content":"Provine Bradley (October 22, 1907 – December 31, 1986) was an American baseball player in the Negro leagues. He played with the Cincinnati Tigers in 1937 and the Memphis Red Sox in 1938. In some sources, his career is combined with that of Frank Bradley.\n\nReferences\n\nExternal links\n and Seamheads\n\nMemphis Red Sox players\nCincinnati Tigers (baseball) players\n1907 births\n1986 deaths\nBaseball players from Louisiana\nBaseball pitchers\nBaseball second basemen\nBaseball outfielders\n20th-century African-American sportspeople\nPeople from Webster Parish, Louisiana","ad_en":[-3.828125,4.390625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.703703703703703,"fineweb_edu":[1.4648699760437012],"modernbert_readability":[-8.71875,-1.921875,-2.06640625,0.84130859375,4.4140625,4.01171875],"qurater":[-2.556640625,-1.2529296875,2.732421875,-1.1220703125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":6.926406926406926,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.90651162,"dsir_math":-720.01531487,"dsir_wiki":-670.82201463,"rps_doc_num_sentences":4,"rps_doc_word_count":81.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-4.28515625,7.6953125,5.98046875,0.7109375,-3.396484375,-6.46875],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":70.0,"fluency_en":[-0.9384765625,1.642578125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":22.898032200357775,"dsir_books":-709.98644864,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-9.546875,-6.5625,7.41796875,6.4296875,6.42578125,-10.1796875],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":22.708515730425727,"modernbert_reasoning":[5.90234375,10.3046875,2.77734375,-4.80078125,-6.19921875,-6.78125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":5,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":23.52941176470588,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":6.132668144863267,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUdiI5qhLA_wzE9RzX","content":"Karl Robert Saluri, né le , est un athlète estonien, spécialiste du décathlon.\n\nCarrière \nIl bat son record personnel avec  points, supérieur au minima pour les Jeux olympiques de Rio, devenant ce faisant le Meilleur athlète européen du mois d'. Son précédent record est battu de 637 points.\nLe , il porte son record personnel à 8137 points lors des NCAA à Eugene.\n\nPalmarès\n\nRecords\n\nRecords personnels\n\nRéférences\n\nLien externe \n \n\nDécathlonien estonien\nNaissance en août 1993\nAthlète (homme) aux Jeux olympiques d'été de 2016","ad_en":[-3.365234375,4.16796875],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.353658536585366,"fineweb_edu":[0.5515490770339966],"modernbert_readability":[-5.51171875,4.06640625,2.603515625,2.455078125,1.1640625,-5.11328125],"qurater":[-1.9892578125,-0.399169921875,1.357421875,-1.822265625],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":4.100227790432802,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":4.01340619,"dsir_math":-814.44098676,"dsir_wiki":-790.28256827,"rps_doc_num_sentences":5,"rps_doc_word_count":82.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.26171875,6.30859375,5.11328125,0.16162109375,-2.650390625,-5.11328125],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":69.38775510204081,"fluency_en":[0.59033203125,-0.289794921875],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":27.272727272727266,"dsir_books":-772.80698102,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-7.25,-7.04296875,5.0625,3.9921875,6.3984375,-4.96875],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":39.46003649868255,"modernbert_reasoning":[3.837890625,10.4453125,4.1484375,-4.30859375,-6.203125,-6.01953125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":8,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":55.00000000000001,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":2.724031039237495,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUbcU5qrqCyihwaLOv","content":"Andreï Vassilievitch Martynov est un paléontologue et entomologiste russe, né le  à Riazan et mort le  à Moscou. Docteur ès sciences en 1933.\n\nBiographie\nIl est diplômé de l'Université d'État de Moscou en 1902 puis assistant au département de zoologie de l'Université de Varsovie en 1909-1915. Conservateur de la section d'entomologie au musée de Zoologie de l'Académie des sciences d'URSS à partir de 1921, il collabore également avec le musée de Géologie de l'Académie des sciences (Léningrad). En 1936, le musée est transféré à Moscou et Martynov vient s'y installer.\n\nIl s'intéresse d'abord aux trichoptères et aux crustacés avant de commencer à s'intéresser aux insectes fossiles.\n\nMort à Moscou, il est inhumé au Cimetière de Novodevitchi.\n\nBibliographie \n Frank M. Carpenter (1938). Andreas Vassilievitch Martynov, Psyche, 45 : 80-83.\n\nNotes et références\n\nLiens externes \n \n \n \n\nEntomologiste de l'Empire russe au XIXe siècle\nEntomologiste de l'Empire russe au XXe siècle\nEntomologiste russe du XXe siècle\nEntomologiste soviétique\nPaléontologue de l'Empire russe au XIXe siècle\nPaléontologue de l'Empire russe au XXe siècle\nPaléontologue russe du XXe siècle\nPaléontologue soviétique\nÉtudiant de l'université d'État de Moscou\nNaissance dans le gouvernement de Riazan\nNaissance à Riazan\nNaissance en août 1879\nDécès en janvier 1938\nDécès à Moscou\nDécès à 58 ans\nPersonnalité inhumée au cimetière de Novodevitchi","ad_en":[-3.48828125,4.06640625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.766666666666667,"fineweb_edu":[1.6156318187713623],"modernbert_readability":[-7.9921875,-3.6328125,-2.10546875,-0.0955810546875,6.0546875,5.0625],"qurater":[-0.74951171875,1.7568359375,1.4990234375,0.46044921875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":2.6424442609413705,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":4.1871539,"dsir_math":-2023.5180833,"dsir_wiki":-1994.79440586,"rps_doc_num_sentences":11,"rps_doc_word_count":210.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-4.90625,