{"id":"BkiUbRI4uBhhxKZ5uOkr","content":"Paratrissocladius lawrencensis is een muggensoort uit de familie van de dansmuggen (Chironomidae). De wetenschappelijke naam van de soort is voor het eerst geldig gepubliceerd in 1988 door Cranston and Oliver.\n\nDansmuggen","ad_en":[-3.30078125,3.890625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":6.0,"fineweb_edu":[0.8513261675834656],"modernbert_readability":[-4.34375,2.640625,0.8798828125,2.083984375,1.5283203125,-2.544921875],"qurater":[-2.822265625,0.392333984375,1.0205078125,-1.123046875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":5.376344086021505,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.12095299,"dsir_math":-337.11876203,"dsir_wiki":-321.95066788,"rps_doc_num_sentences":3,"rps_doc_word_count":31.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.287109375,1.556640625,3.6875,2.18359375,0.08526611328125,-3.3203125],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":80.64516129032258,"fluency_en":[-0.04107666015625,0.40185546875],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":17.64705882352942,"dsir_books":-320.94483122,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-9.328125,-9.75,4.41015625,2.587890625,9.9921875,-5.9921875],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":37.46411483253589,"modernbert_reasoning":[7.37109375,9.65625,1.2744140625,-4.8515625,-5.53515625,-5.63671875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":66.66666666666666,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":0.975609756097561,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUcj_xK4tBVhvvrmff","content":"Joseph-Pierre Louveau (1744-1822), homme politique français ;\n Jean Louveau (1871-1906), religieux français ;\n Edmond Louveau (1895-1973), fonctionnaire et résistant français, Compagnon de la Libération ;\n Henri Louveau (1910-1991), pilote automobile français ;\n Catherine Louveau (née en 1950), sociologue française.","ad_en":[-3.6171875,4.35546875],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":7.3428571428571425,"fineweb_edu":[1.1025607585906982],"modernbert_readability":[-7.7109375,-0.0460205078125,-1.9072265625,1.1845703125,2.572265625,2.615234375],"qurater":[-0.49462890625,-0.1790771484375,0.479736328125,-1.87890625],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":0.0,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.16699472,"dsir_math":-550.56615191,"dsir_wiki":-535.77436568,"rps_doc_num_sentences":1,"rps_doc_word_count":35.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-4.89453125,11.5,4.94921875,-0.7861328125,-4.3671875,-6.875],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":74.4186046511628,"fluency_en":[-1.939453125,1.953125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":35.33123028391168,"dsir_books":-554.7852009,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-8.5078125,2.00390625,11.1953125,1.65625,1.0849609375,-9.6328125],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":4.127292658509959,"modernbert_reasoning":[11.03125,8.96875,-1.205078125,-5.67578125,-6.4140625,-5.68359375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":20.0,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":13.347744280931456,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUdW025V5irJ1XxM43","content":"Junge Philharmonie steht für:\n Junge Deutsche Philharmonie \n Junge Münchner Philharmonie\n Junge Norddeutsche Philharmonie\n Junge Philharmonie Brandenburg\n Junge Philharmonie Köln\n Junge Philharmonie Salzburg\n Junge Philharmonie Erlangen","ad_en":[-3.005859375,3.78515625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":8.24,"fineweb_edu":[0.4950694739818573],"modernbert_readability":[-7.90234375,0.689453125,-1.064453125,2.193359375,1.087890625,2.791015625],"qurater":[-0.90673828125,-0.45751953125,-0.724609375,-0.46630859375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":41.262135922330096,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":1.88803324,"dsir_math":-334.61211396,"dsir_wiki":-335.60305005,"rps_doc_num_sentences":1,"rps_doc_word_count":25.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.205078125,9.3828125,5.56640625,-1.2333984375,-3.716796875,-6.60546875],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":50.0,"fluency_en":[-1.1748046875,1.5439453125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":15.254237288135599,"dsir_books":-339.62112777,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-8.8828125,4.94140625,13.015625,0.38623046875,0.486328125,-12.7421875],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":10.117081976005084,"modernbert_reasoning":[9.6328125,9.625,1.05078125,-4.78515625,-6.4375,-6.69140625],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":0.0,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":0.0,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUbDU5jDKDyDAe7x4-","content":"Ку́кка () — деревня в волости Хийумаа уезда Хийумаа, Эстония.\n\nДо реформы местных самоуправлений 2017 года входила в состав волости Пюхалепа.\n\nГеография \nРасположена в северо-восточной части острова Хийумаа. Расстояние до волостного и уездного центра — города Кярдла —  6 километров. Высота над уровнем моря — 6 метров.\n\nМалые острова в заливе Кукка относятся к деревне Кылунымме.\n\nНаселение \nПо данным переписи населения 2011 года, в деревне проживали 11 человек, все — эстонцы.\n\nПо состоянию на 1 января 2020 года в деревне насчитывалось 28 жителей: 11 женщин и 17 мужчин; 23 человека трудоспособного возраста (15–64 года), 1 ребёнок в возрасте до 15 лет и 4 человека пенсионного возраста (65 лет и старше).\n\nЧисленность населения деревни Кукка:\n\nИстория \nВ письменных источниках 1565 года упоминается Kucku, 1609 года — Kucku Wackan, Kucku Peter, 1688 года — Kuckaby, Kukkuby, 1782 года — Kuckas, 1798 года — Kukka.\n\nНа военно-топографических картах Российской империи (1846–1863 годы), в состав которой входила Эстляндская губерния, деревня обозначена как Кукка.\n\nДостопримечательности \n\n Камень Кукка\nКрупнейший эрратический валун Западной Эстонии, гранит, объём наземной части 324 м3;\n природный парк Кукка\nРасположен к югу от деревни, площадь 1,5 км2. Основан в 1998 году для защиты низинного болота и его биоразнообразия. Здесь растёт множество охраняемых видов растений, в частности, лосняк Лёзеля, офрис насекомоносная, пальчатокоренник мясо-красный, дремлик болотный и кокушник комарниковый;\n ветряная мельница Кукка\nПостроена в 1837 году. Классический тип деревянной ветряной мельницы, памятник культуры, символ истории местного сельскохозяйственного производства. При инспектировании 30.08.2016 состояние оценивалось как хорошее.\n\nПримечания \n\nНаселённые пункты Эстонии\nХийумаа","ad_en":[-2.220703125,2.515625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":6.139344262295082,"fineweb_edu":[0.7783681154251099],"modernbert_readability":[-5.34375,-1.11328125,0.3583984375,0.78515625,3.16015625,0.5146484375],"qurater":[-2.640625,-2.119140625,0.12274169921875,-1.33984375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":1.335113484646195,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":4.9421891,"dsir_math":-1982.96759485,"dsir_wiki":-1918.95887261,"rps_doc_num_sentences":18,"rps_doc_word_count":244.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.9140625,2.48046875,3.083984375,1.80078125,-0.72021484375,-3.13671875],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":74.8,"fluency_en":[1.16796875,-1.0859375],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":97.15083798882682,"dsir_books":-1957.79782926,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-5.5625,-4.0234375,0.5908203125,-2.96484375,4.58203125,4.64453125],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":39.19046596143257,"modernbert_reasoning":[-0.0697021484375,7.31640625,4.01171875,-2.134765625,-3.76171875,-4.53125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":1,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":61.76470588235294,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":2.516729261135532,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUdNU5qYVBUVZOitKJ","content":"Nanying may refer to:\n\n Nanying, Gaocheng District, a town in Gaocheng District, Shijiazhuang, Hebei, China\n Nanying Township, a township in Lingshou County, Shijiazhuang, Hebei, China\n Nanying Subdistrict (南营街道), a subdistrict of Yicheng, Hubei, China\n\nSee also\nNanyin (disambiguation)","ad_en":[-3.6796875,4.47265625],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":5.973684210526316,"fineweb_edu":[0.7073371410369873],"modernbert_readability":[-9.1328125,-2.18359375,-2.232421875,0.69580078125,3.763671875,6.3046875],"qurater":[-3.3203125,-1.9736328125,0.62353515625,-1.330078125],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":14.096916299559473,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.06282533,"dsir_math":-476.75652203,"dsir_wiki":-454.5707697,"rps_doc_num_sentences":1,"rps_doc_word_count":38.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-4.0,9.703125,5.9765625,-0.262939453125,-3.701171875,-7.4609375],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":63.1578947368421,"fluency_en":[-2.2265625,2.064453125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":22.027972027972027,"dsir_books":-465.04218811,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-10.7109375,-5.76953125,10.1015625,1.1181640625,5.06640625,-6.53515625],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":30.97584415695306,"modernbert_reasoning":[9.2578125,10.8359375,0.7607421875,-5.4296875,-6.703125,-6.859375],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":19,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":25.0,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_fraction":0.0,"sub_path":"","_source_domain":"wikipedia","_source_path":"wikipedia/part-6777d8857c6e-000341.jsonl"}
{"id":"BkiUcGvxK02iP15vfR5o","content":"Abaixo estão citados as embaixadas e/ou consulados de Djibouti:\n\nEuropa\n\nBruxelas (Embaixada)\n\nParis (Embaixada)\n\nGenebra (Embaixada)\n\nAmérica\n\n Montreal (Consulado)\n\n Washington DC (Embaixada)\n\nOriente Médio\n\nDoa (Embaixada)\n\nRiade (Embaixada)\nJedá (Consulado-Geral)\n\nAbu Dabi (Embaixada)\nDubai (Consulado-Geral)\n\nSaná (Embaixada)\n\nÁfrica\n\nCairo (Embaixada)\n\nAsmara (Embaixada)\n\n Adis-Abeba (Embaixada)\n Dire Dawa (Consulado-Geral)\n\n Casablanca (Consulado)\n\n Cartum (Embaixada)\n\n Mogadíscio (Embaixada)\n\nÁsia\n\nPequim (Embaixada)\n\nNova Déli (Embaixada)\n\nTóquio (Embaixada)\n\nOrganizações multilaterais\n Nova Iorque (Delegação antes as Nações Unidas)\n\nLigações externas \nMinistério das relações exteriores de Djibouti\n\nDjibouti\nPolítica do Djibouti\nListas do Djibouti\nDjibouti","ad_en":[-1.7060546875,1.98828125],"rps_doc_mean_word_length":7.27906976744186,"fineweb_edu":[0.4941532611846924],"modernbert_readability":[-5.92578125,0.1304931640625,0.334716796875,1.228515625,2.189453125,-0.0712890625],"qurater":[-3.56640625,-0.44287109375,0.343505859375,-2.044921875],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_2gram":3.1948881789137378,"rps_doc_unigram_entropy":3.69458817,"dsir_math":-1227.10255672,"dsir_wiki":-1244.71217595,"rps_doc_num_sentences":1,"rps_doc_word_count":86.0,"modernbert_professionalism":[-3.3359375,6.76171875,4.59375,0.177978515625,-2.451171875,-5.2421875],"rps_doc_frac_unique_words":64.15094339622641,"fluency_en":[-0.1510009765625,0.25830078125],"rps_doc_frac_no_alph_words":24.8062015503876,"dsir_books":-1246.87564901,"modernbert_cleanliness":[-6.69921875,0.55615234375,11.3359375,4.19921875,0.64501953125,-12.8984375],"rps_lines_uppercase_letter_fraction":49.3899197463744,"modernbert_reasoning":[8.015625,9.2109375,1.099609375,-5.13671875,-5.82421875,-5.84765625],"rps_doc_frac_chars_top_3gram":0,"rps_lines_ending_with_terminal_punctution_mark":42.62295081967213,"rps_lines_numerical_chars_f